      "reasoning": "I'll cast Trusty Retriever. For {3}{W}, I get a 3/3 that can return a creature from my graveyard when it enters. My Feat of Resistance is in the graveyard, but there's no target to return it to — and it's an instant, not a creature. However, later on, if I get a creature like Mesa Unicorn or Inspiriring Unicorn in the graveyard, I can retrieve it. The immediate value is the 3/3 body, which is a solid threat. I'm prioritizing tempo and incremental advantage.\n\
\n\
I could cast Secure the Scene for two 1/1s and a life gain, but Trusty Retriever has more long-term value and scales better, especially with multiple Thriving Heaths for life gain.\n\
\n\
Cast Trusty Retriever now.\n\
