      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Emiel the Blessed and Angel of Flight Alabaster have trading in combat — both died.\n\
\n\
I lost Emiel, but that’s fine — it served its purpose. It was a 4/4 body and I got value.\n\
\n\
More importantly, Mesa Unicorn and Trusty Retriever dealt 3 and 3 unblocked damage, dropping my opponent from 14 to 8 life. \n\
\n\
Additionally, Cathar's Companion has lifelink — but it didn't attack, so no lifelink trigger.\n\
\n\
Wait — did any of my attackers have lifelink? Mesa Unicorn has lifelink.\n\
\n\
Yes! Mesa Unicorn is a 3/3 with lifelink — it dealt 3 unblocked damage, so I gain 3 life.\n\
\n\
I was at 22 — now I'm at 25.\n\
\n\
Mesa Unicorn survived — it wasn't blocked.\n\
\n\
So battlefield: I have Mesa Unicorn (3/3 lifelink, +1/+1=1), Trusty Retriever (3/4, +1/+1=1), Cathar's Companion (4/2, +1/+1=1), and two Thriving Heaths.\n\
\n\
I'm at 25 life.\n\
\n\
Opponent is at 8 life, with no creatures except Amoeboid Changeling and Eidolon of Rhetoric.\n\
\n\
They have Gigantoplasm in graveyard — they could potentially copy one of my creatures, but not immediately.\n\
\n\
I still have a postcombat main phase.\n\
\n\
I can cast another spell — but Eidolon of Rhetoric restricts me to one spell per turn, and I already cast Cathar's Companion.\n\
\n\
So I cannot cast anything.\n\
\n\
No actions possible.\n\
\n\
Pass priority to end turn.\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
