      "reasoning": "Mirror Image was used to copy Eidolon of Rhetoric? That's what the battlefield shows — two Eidolon of Rhetoric.\n\
\n\
But only one is tapped? Or both are present.\n\
\n\
Wait — battlefield shows two Eidolon of Rhetoric: one tapped and one not, both 1/4.\n\
\n\
But only one was there before. So Mirror Image copied it.\n\
\n\
That means they now have two copies of \"Each player can't cast more than one spell each turn.\"\n\
\n\
That's a problem — it doesn't stack; it's a replacement effect. But having two is redundant — the rule still applies once.\n\
\n\
More importantly, it means they can't cast another spell this turn, which limits them.\n\
\n\
But they also used their one spell on the copy.\n\
\n\
Now is my turn.\n\
\n\
I passed priority last turn, so now it's my precombat main phase.\n\
\n\
I have one land drop remaining.\n\
\n\
Do I have a land in hand? Hand: Affa Guard Hound, Inspiring Unicorn, Release the Dogs, Secure the Scene — all spells, no land.\n\
\n\
So I can't play a land.\n\
\n\
I can cast one spell — Cathar’s Companion resolved last turn, so this turn I can cast one.\n\
\n\
I have multiple options:\n\
\n\
- **Inspiring Unicorn** ({2}{W}{W}) — makes my creatures +1/+1 when it attacks.\n\
- **Affa Guard Hound** ({2}{W}) — flash, +0/+3 to a creature.\n\
- **Release the Dogs** ({3}{W}) — four 1/1 Dog tokens.\n\
- **Secure the Scene** ({4}{W}) — exile a nonland permanent, they get a Soldier.\n\
\n\
The best play depends on board state.\n\
\n\
Opponent has:\n\
- Amoeboid Changeling (1/1)\n\
- Two Eidolon of Rhetoric (1/4, one tapped)\n\
- Heirloom Blade\n\
- No creatures with toughness >1 that are relevant.\n\
\n\
They can't cast more than one spell per turn, so they're severely limited.\n\
\n\
But they do have Gigantoplasm in graveyard — they could play it to copy one of my creatures.\n\
\n\
But they can only cast one spell, so if they don't have it in hand, they can't.\n\
\n\
Right now, their hand is 1 card — likely Gigantoplasm or a counterspell.\n\
\n\
Best to apply pressure.\n\
\n\
Inspiring Unicorn is strong — when it attacks, all my creatures get +1/+1. With Cathar’s Companion, Mesa Unicorn, and Trusty Retriever, that's four creatures — they all become 1/1 bigger.\n\
\n\
Plus, it’s a 2/2, and I have Emiel in graveyard — I can’t get value now.\n\
\n\
Affa Guard Hound is flash, but I’d rather not waste the flash unless needed.\n\
\n\
Release the Dogs gives me four bodies — useful for chump blocking or overwhelming.\n\
\n\
Secure the Scene exiles a permanent — but exiling one Eidolon doesn’t stop the other.\n\
\n\
And they get a Soldier token — I don’t want to give them a creature.\n\
\n\
So best to go wide or buff.\n\
\n\
I have big creatures — Trusty Retriever is 4/5 with +1/+1, Mesa Unicorn 4/4 lifelink, Cathar’s Companion 5/3 lifelink after buff.\n\
\n\
Inspiring Unicorn will make them all bigger and enable lethal.\n\
\n\
I’ll cast Inspiring Unicorn.\n\
\n\
Tap two Plains and a Thriving Heath ({W}) for {2}{W}{W}.\n\
\n\
Cast Inspiring Unicorn.\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
